            <ArticleTitle>[Anti-ischemic efficacy of combination of trimetazidine with enalapril in patients with stable effort angina and metabolic syndrome].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>17-22</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Efficacy of combination of trimetazidine (60 mg/day) and enalapril in patients with stable effort angina and metabolic syndrome was assessed in a randomized placebo controlled study of 64 patients. Anti-ischemic activity of trimetazidine was found to be significant. It was most pronounced in patients with abnormal 24-hour blood pressure index, waist/hip circumference ratio &gt;1.0 at the background of satisfactory clinical and laboratory compensation of type 2 diabetes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
